Hi Ai,

Good to hear from you!  Based on your model specifications, I wouldn't think that model should take that long to run.  One key thing can be adding bounds to free parameters.  The current optimizer (SLSQP) usually takes insanely large steps and needs to walk them back which can waste a lot of time.

I look further into your example though.

Cheers,
Mike

