Hi Ai,

The scripts RSLinearDiscrete.R and RSLinearDiscreteYang.R have examples of setting upper and lower bounds. In the snippet of code below, it shows how you can add an upper bound (use lb for lower bound) of 1.1 to the parameters phi_1 and phi_2. Another weird thing though. If you want a VAR model, it is discrete time. So you should set isContinuousTime=FALSE in prep.formulaDynamics. Finally, the starting values you used seem to be in the non-stationary range. Shouldn't be a problem, but may take longer for the program to bounce back. Try setting the starting values for all cross-regression parameters to be 0s.

Sy-Miin

rsmod <- dynr.model(
  dynamics = recDyn,
  measurement = recMeas,
  noise = recNoise,
  initial = recIni,
  regimes = recReg,
  data = EMGdata)
#  outfile = "RSLinearDiscrete.c")

rsmod$ub[c('phi_1', 'phi_2')] <- 1.1

